						<tr>
							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left"><b>The thought of losing our name are having to take the name of another server really burns me up. </b><br /><br />(I still can&#039;t understand why this would &quot;REALLY BURN YOU UP&quot;) I understand that you may feel the need to merge (I dont think we need it) but make BOTH servers change their name. <br /><br />This is going to cause a lot of resentment from both servers RN peeps are going to hate haveing to be moved and the people from Q are gonna hate having to compete with guilds from RN (this is going to be a big PITA) becaue <b>Q people are going to feel like they own the server and RN people are going to be beligerent about not having to do thing they way they are done on Q. </b><br /><br />How does one &quot;feel like they own the server&quot; ? Maybe if there was PVP or something, yeah, I could see some impact. As is, the only interaction we could possibly have is spamming chat or pulling mobs from your camp. And since every really nice zone for loot is instanced, I don&#039;t even see how this is an issue.<br /><br />As far as RN people being belligerent, I can&#039;t really understand what is said there either. Not having to do thing they way they are done on Q? That kinda mean Quellians aren&#039;t going to follow a rotation? On what, instanced poTime? Haha! Ah well, guess the joke&#039;s on me for being too ignorant about having a fetal attachment syndrome for my servername. *shrug*<br /><br />Personally, the only thing that I believe would piss people off the most would be forcing them to change names due to simliar toons on the server. That&#039;s the ONLY problem I see. But I don&#039;t see anyone whining about that... again, I guess my association with a toon is based on the name, not the server. Probably because I don&#039;t have a cool name, like Mitcheypoo Poodedoo (or i&#039;d damn sure wanna change names!).<br /><br />I know a lot of you Rodcet Nife players are looking forward to the merger, and it appears all the retired people are the complainers here. Obviously, I don&#039;t care much about the retired folk. I mean, wow, you&#039;re still reading messageboards about a game you quit how many years ago? Don&#039;t tell me it&#039;s the camaraderie, since whining about servernames isn&#039;t related to the fellowship of players long since gone.<br /><br />Irregardless, I anticipate the merging of OUR server, whatever the name may become.</td>
